  "drivers": "Nasdaq-100 futures are down about 1.1% while Dow futures slip 0.2% and Russell 2000 futures edge up 0.3%. Alphabet is down ~11% pre-market after Q3 search-ad results disappointed and it reported negative free cash flow (about −$9.1B) on accelerating AI spending; Microsoft is up ~2% on an Azure-driven beat, while CoreWeave and Nebius slide. Software is hit hard: ServiceNow −19% (EPS miss) and Fortinet −26% (slower service revenue growth) drag Palo Alto, CrowdStrike and Zscaler lower. The Fed held at 3.75%–4.00% on Wednesday after its September hike; futures price high odds of a December hike. At 7:30 a.m. CT, Q3 GDP came in at 3.4% (est. 3.2%) and September PCE inflation matched estimates (headline 3.6% y/y, core 3.1% y/y, core +0.3% m/m); personal income +0.2% and spending +0.5% were slightly light. DoorDash agreed to buy Instacart for $17B; Lilly, Caterpillar, Mastercard and Merck reported before the open, with Amazon and Intel after the close.",
